From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:50:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add Athena.addPinnedChunks: pin another square of a world

A match map whose deathmatch arena lies away from its centre could only be pinned as one square
big enough for both, which also made the land between them exist. addPinnedChunks adds a square
to the world's pinned area and keeps the ones before; pinChunks still replaces them all, and
unpinChunks ends them all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java b/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
index bc07357e89b50104cc468960f0a605b54a0fcb1a..151be5551a6b9b44bc9ccfee66a48cc8a7e74763 100644
--- a/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
+++ b/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@ public final class Athena {
      * soon, the radius is too small.
      *
      * <p>Pin before players enter the world: a chunk already in a player's view when the square is
-     * set or changed keeps what it had. Pinning again replaces the world's previous square.
+     * set or changed keeps what it had. Pinning again replaces the world's previous squares; {@link #addPinnedChunks} adds one instead.
      *
      * <p>Meant for a match map: a chunk is read once per match instead of again each time players
      * come back to it, its changes stay (on a template world an unloaded chunk loses them), and
@@ -136,6 +136,27 @@ public final class Athena {
         getServer().pinChunks(center, radius);
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Adds the square of {@code radius} blocks around {@code center} to {@code center}'s world's
+     * pinned area, keeping the squares pinned before; the world is then every pinned square, and
+     * chunks outside all of them do not exist, as with {@link #pinChunks}. Pins the square alone if
+     * the world has no pin.
+     *
+     * <p>Meant for a part of a match map away from the main square, such as a deathmatch arena: pin
+     * the main square with {@link #pinChunks}, then add the arena, instead of one square big enough
+     * for both (which would also make the land between them exist). As with {@link #pinChunks}, make
+     * the square the area players there may see, and add it before players enter the world: a chunk
+     * already in a player's view when the square is added keeps what it had.
+     * {@link #unpinChunks} ends every square at once.
+     *
+     * @param center the middle of the square, and the world
+     * @param radius half the square's side, in blocks
+     * @throws IllegalArgumentException if {@code center} has no world or {@code radius} is negative
+     */
+    public static void addPinnedChunks(Location center, int radius) {
+        getServer().addPinnedChunks(center, radius);
+    }
+
     /**
      * Ends {@code world}'s pin, if it has one; the chunks it kept that no player is using are
      * queued to unload as usual.
diff --git a/src/main/java/athena/api/AthenaServer.java b/src/main/java/athena/api/AthenaServer.java
index 493d059b0b62e522dcf2d216052e8c828ef0a4bf..0b6e7fd29cc01abe3b20abb4abd621d047793ea7 100644
--- a/src/main/java/athena/api/AthenaServer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/athena/api/AthenaServer.java
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@ public interface AthenaServer {
 
     void pinChunks(Location center, int radius);
 
+    void addPinnedChunks(Location center, int radius);
+
     void unpinChunks(World world);
 
     CompletableFuture<Integer> preloadChunks(Location center, int radius, int perTick);
